  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I want one regulatory network per patient for our 85 ovarian tumours from the expression matrix with motif and PPI priors; a TargetScan-based miRNA prior and a miRNA list are also on hand. I'm not sure yet whether the regulators should be just transcription factors or also microRNAs."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Before I choose a workflow, please tell me:\n- Do you want the regulators to include microRNAs as well?\n  You wrote: \"I'm not sure yet whether the regulators should be just transcription factors or also microRNAs\". LIONESS-PANDA's contract: \"LIONESS-PANDA uses the original gene-by-sample expression matrix, motif and PPI priors to internally infer the aggregate PANDA network and derive sample-specific TF-to-gene networks\".\n\nNo workflow has been selected and nothing runs before you answer.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Previous NetZoo goal: I want one regulatory network per patient for our 85 ovarian tumours from the expression matrix with motif and PPI priors; a TargetScan-based miRNA prior and a miRNA list are also on hand. I'm not sure yet whether the regulators should be just transcription factors or also microRNAs.\nUser follow-up: Transcription factors only."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I want one regulatory network per patient for our 85 ovarian tumours from the expression matrix with motif and PPI priors; a TargetScan-based miRNA prior and a miRNA list are also on hand.\" -- available from LIONESS-PANDA.\n\nSelected path: **LIONESS-PANDA**.\n\nYour question asks for a per-sample regulatory network. **LIONESS-PANDA** fits that result and scale.\n\n**LIONESS-PANDA** — Infer aggregate PANDA and sample-specific LIONESS-PANDA networks. LIONESS represents the cohort network through sample contributions: W_q = N*W_all - (N-1)*W_without_q, where N is the cohort size and the same base estimator is fitted with and without sample q. The leave-one-out network alone is not the patient's network. This borrows cohort information; it does not estimate a correlation from one isolated observation or prove causality. With PANDA, edge weights are inferred regulatory support, not measured binding strength. Cross-sectional networks do not establish temporal rewiring. Message passing iteratively reconciles a regulator-target prior with other biological evidence networks. Other evidence can revise the initial edge support, but the resulting weights are integrated network scores, not calibrated posterior probabilities of prior reliability.\n\nRequired workflow inputs:\n\n- `expression_file`: expression matrix\n- `motif_file`: motif/prior\n- `ppi_file`: PPI network\n\nCost: LIONESS runs PANDA once on all samples and once more without each sample, so N samples take N+1 PANDA runs and give N network files. Plan the runtime and disk space, and filter edges before downstream statistics.\n\nOutputs:\n\n- `regulatory_network`: Inferred regulator-to-target associations.\n\nOut-degree measures how strongly a TF is wired to its targets in each sample. If you mean TF activity instead -- how active a TF is apart from its own mRNA level -- GIRAFFE's TF-by-sample activity matrix is the other reading, from the expression, motif and PPI inputs.\n\nAsk for the workflow's controls and defaults if you want to set them.\n\nThis is workflow guidance only; no execution was authorized. No files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
